From: Shivam-Sharma <shivamsharmaxd43@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 13:44:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] docs: fix contradictions found while building an adapter

- codex README: a heuristic warning does exist; lifecycle timeouts per event
- 06-file-patterns: six matcher shapes, not five
- bug template: build string is +release.<sha>
- README: adk-pin applies to every pin-file ADK host
- HOST-PROFILES: point to the host-adapter issue template

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TnQvGeyaju6t8dVH4gy5it
---
 .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug-report.yml         |  2 +-
 README.md                                     |  2 +-
 adapter-toolkit/HOST-PROFILES.md              |  2 +-
 adapter-toolkit/reference/codex/README.md     | 10 ++++++----
 examples/policies/fields/06-file-patterns.lua |  2 +-
 5 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug-report.yml b/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug-report.yml
index 4e8ef6e..459d0ae 100644
--- a/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug-report.yml
+++ b/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug-report.yml
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ body:
     attributes:
       label: Version
       description: Output of `isonapse --version`
-      placeholder: isonapse 0.3.0-beta+main.abc1234
+      placeholder: isonapse 0.3.0-beta+release.abc1234
     validations:
       required: true
   - type: dropdown
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index ca39fe0..5a836ce 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -194,7 +194,7 @@ restart approves every monitored file as it then is.
 
     brew upgrade isonapse        # or rerun the script installer
     isonapse hook restart        # moves the daemon onto the installed build
-    isonapse hook adk-pin        # Codex CLI only: re-pin the upgraded Hook
+    isonapse hook adk-pin        # ADK hosts with a pin file (e.g. Codex CLI): re-pin the upgraded Hook
     isonapse hook status
 
 After an authorized personal-plugin upgrade, rerun `isonapse hook init` once
diff --git a/adapter-toolkit/HOST-PROFILES.md b/adapter-toolkit/HOST-PROFILES.md
index b446b69..9beb2e9 100644
--- a/adapter-toolkit/HOST-PROFILES.md
+++ b/adapter-toolkit/HOST-PROFILES.md
@@ -206,7 +206,7 @@ does not attest imported modules, plugins or already loaded code. The operator
 must control and review the whole runtime installation. File pins and process
 identity do not isolate malicious code running as the installation owner.
 
-To add a host, open a public feature request containing:
+To add a host, open an issue with the "Host adapter or profile" template containing:
 
 - upstream host/project and version range;
 - stable session and tool-call identity sources;
diff --git a/adapter-toolkit/reference/codex/README.md b/adapter-toolkit/reference/codex/README.md
index 5bd5be5..1fc86ec 100644
--- a/adapter-toolkit/reference/codex/README.md
+++ b/adapter-toolkit/reference/codex/README.md
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ update.
 | Approval (`ask`) | **no**: Codex parses `ask` but does not support it and lets the tool run | never declared; an `ask` is a deny |
 | Output replacement | **no exact replacement**: PostToolUse can only withhold a result | never declared; any required replacement or refusal is `decision:"block"` |
 | Prompt boundary | not wired | not declared |
-| Lifecycle | SessionStart, SessionEnd (advisory, 1-3 s budget) | acknowledged; cannot block |
+| Lifecycle | SessionStart (60 s, two 25 s exchanges), SessionEnd (advisory, Codex caps it at 3 s) | acknowledged; cannot block |
 
 Register the profile with `--input-replacement` only. Codex keeps the raw
 tool result when a PostToolUse hook withholds it; the model sees the block
@@ -413,9 +413,11 @@ and is logged only at info level.
   later hook's rewrite are invisible before the effect.
 - PostToolUse fires for commands that exit non-zero (the result is bound and
   witnessed) but not when Codex itself failed to run the tool.
-- Nothing warns you when a registered Codex host stops being governed, for
-  example after an edit of its definitions left them untrusted (observed on
-  codex-cli 0.155.1, not a maintained test).
+- Only a heuristic warns you when a registered Codex host stops being
+  governed, for example after an edit of its definitions left them untrusted
+  (observed on codex-cli 0.155.1, not a maintained test): `hook status` and
+  `hook report --host` flag a changed `hooks.json` with no tool decision since
+  (see "Upgrade" above). A host that runs no hooks leaves no other trace.
 
 ## Proven
 
diff --git a/examples/policies/fields/06-file-patterns.lua b/examples/policies/fields/06-file-patterns.lua
index c10175c..f096d4e 100644
--- a/examples/policies/fields/06-file-patterns.lua
+++ b/examples/policies/fields/06-file-patterns.lua
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 --    Useful for blocking accidental megabyte-scale writes from agents
 --    that thought they were appending a line.
 --
--- The matcher is intentionally NARROW (no full regex). Five shapes:
+-- The matcher is intentionally NARROW (no full regex). Six shapes:
 --
 --   name             — bare basename match (no slashes).
 --   **/name          — any path whose final component equals `name`.
